Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='storemarks', at=datetime(2026, 11, 22, 15, 55, 5, 954317), actor='assistant', title='A store is read by the mark of its last hold, so every writer of a live store moves together', body="A STORE IS READ BY ITS MARK (2026-11-22): from the store library pinned at `85e5083`, every hold of a store's lock writes a fresh mark (`.writes`, local to one machine and named by the store's `.gitignore`), and a handle that has read a store reads it again by comparing marks, not by listing `objects/`. So whatever changes `objects/` without the lock is a door the store does not see until its next hold: a `git pull`, merge or restore of the data tree, and a write by a binary of another pin. The rules that follow: a live store is written only by a binary at the deployed pin; `scripts/deploy.sh` proves each store's `.gitignore` is in its present form (`migrate-ignores --check`), waits for runs of the other app, pauses the timers and the mail watcher, looks again after the stop and after the link, restarts the units, records every store's heads, starts the paused units again and ends non-zero naming any that did not start; after a pull, merge or restore, `scripts/app-bin.sh --deployed prodrome record` records the heads and `verify` names a store left behind; a write by a binary of another pin leaves a correct record of heads that a warm server does not read, so its cure is a restart of the server. A store's doors are a fact of its kind (`Kind::doors`): a plugin's and a provider's cache stores are their program's alone, every other store is shared and lists at each write.", rationale="Decided 2026-11-22 with the pin of the store library: a warm read without a listing is what makes a conversation's read cost microseconds, and it is sound only while every writer moves the mark. The first plan of the move would have stopped every data push at its own landing, so the transition was made in two releases (the stores' ignore lines first, then the pin).", supersedes=()))